hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18258","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came early to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi asking him about wiping over the leather socks, so he said: What brought you. I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings, and he raised the hadith to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"18259","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us, Zirr ibn Hubaysh narrated to me, he said: I came as a delegate during the caliphate of Uthman ibn Affan, and what prompted me to come was meeting Ubayy ibn Kab and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I met Safwan ibn Assal and said to him: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Yes, and I raided with him twelve expeditions."
"18260","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Asim from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi and asked him about wiping over the leather socks, so he said: We would be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would order us not to remove our socks for three days except from major impurity, but from stool and urine and sleep."
"18261","And a loud-voiced Bedouin came and said: O Muhammad, a man loves a people but has not yet joined them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves."
"18262","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, and Yazid narrated it to us, Shubah informed us from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Salamah narrating from Safwan ibn Assal, Yazid said al-Muradi, he said: A Jew said to his companion: Go with us to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Yazid said to this Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that we may ask him about this verse: And We gave Musa nine signs. So he said: Do not say to him prophet, for if he hears you he will gain four eyes. So they asked him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor practice sorcery, nor consume usury, nor take an innocent one to a ruler that he may kill him, nor slander a chaste woman, or he said flee from battle, Shubah the doubter, and you, O Jews, particularly must not transgress, Yazid said transgress on the Sabbath. So they kissed his hand and his foot, Yazid said his hands and his feet, and said: We bear witness that you are a prophet. He said: Then what prevents you from following me. They said: Dawud, peace be upon him, prayed that there would always be a prophet among his progeny, and we fear, Yazid said if we accept Islam the Jews will kill us."
"18263","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi and he said: What brought you. He said: So I said: I came seeking knowledge. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one goes out of a house seeking knowledge but the angels lay their wings for him, pleased with what he does."
"18264","He said: I came to ask you about wiping over the leather socks. He said: Yes, I was in the army which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent, and he ordered us to wipe over the leather socks when we had put them on in purity, three days when traveling and a day and night when resident, and not to remove them except from major impurity."
"18265","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: In the west is an open door for repentance, its travel distance seventy years, not closed until the sun rises from its direction."
"18266","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr informed us from Abu Rawq al-Hamdani that Abu al-Gharif narrated to them, he said: Safwan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition. He said: Proceed in the name of Allah in the cause of Allah, fighting the enemies of Allah. Do not steal spoils and do not kill a child."
"18267","And for the traveler three days and their nights wiping over his leather socks when he inserts his feet in purity, and for the resident a day and night."
"18268","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us, he heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi and he said: What brought you. So I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: The angels lay their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks."
"18269","I said: Wiping over the leather socks stirred in my mind, and Sufyan once said or in my chest, after stool and urine, and you were a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to ask whether you heard anything of that from him. He said: Yes, he used to order us when we were traveling to not remove our socks for three days and their nights except from major impurity, but from stool and urine and sleep."
"18270","He said: I said to him: Did you hear him mention love. He said: Yes, while we were with him on a journey a loud-voiced Bedouin called him saying: O Muhammad. So we said: Woe to you, lower your voice, for you have been forbidden that. So he said: By Allah, I will not lower my voice. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Here, and answered him similarly to his question, and Sufyan once said and answered him similarly to what he said, saying: What of a man who loves a people but has not yet joined them. He said: He is with whom he loves."
"18271","He said: Then he kept narrating to us until he said: From the direction of the west is a door whose width is seventy or forty years travel, which Allah Almighty opened for repentance on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and He will not close it until the sun rises from it."
"18272","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah, Amr ibn Murrah narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Salamah from Safwan ibn Assal, he said: A man from the Jews said to another: Take us to this Prophet. He said: Do not say this, for if he heard it he would gain four eyes. He said: So we went to him and asked him about this verse: And We gave Musa nine clear signs. He said: Do not associate anything with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor flee from battle, nor practice sorcery, nor consume usury, nor hand an innocent one to a ruler that he may kill him, and upon you particularly, O Jews, not to transgress on the Sabbath. So they said: We bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah."
"18273","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Rawq Atiyyah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abu al-Gharif narrated to us, Affan said Abu al-Gharif Abdullah ibn Khalifah, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition and said: Raid in the name of Allah in the cause of Allah, and do not steal spoils, nor betray, nor mutilate, nor kill a child."
"18274","For the traveler three days wiping over the leather socks, and for the resident a day and night. Affan said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me."
"18275","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad that is Ibn Salamah narrated to us from Asim from Zirr from Safwan ibn Assal that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he sought."
"18276","Surayj narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us from Abu Rawq Atiyyah ibn al-Harith, Abdullah ibn Khalifah narrated to us from Safwan ibn Assal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition and mentioned the like of the hadith of Yunus."
"18277","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi and he said: What brought you. So I said: Seeking knowledge. So he said: It has reached me that the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he does. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"18278","So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: A person is with whom he loves."
"18279","He said: And he kept narrating to me until he narrated to me that Allah Almighty placed in the west a door whose width is seventy years travel for repentance, not closed so long as the sun has not risen from its direction, and that is the saying of Allah Almighty: On the day some signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith."
